--- show-card refusals for a recorded gate
    show-card.sh: a recorded gate needs --effort, an absolute folder
    show-card.sh: --record must be lowercase words joined by dashes
    show-card.sh: a recorded gate needs --accept, the option that means yes
--- a recorded gate: the question must be one, single-select, offering the yes option
    A recorded gate asks exactly one question.
    A recorded gate asks a single-select question.
    The question must offer the yes option the card named: Approve the spec (Recommended)
  the good question: allowed, a hand-off left
    [no output = allowed]
    t1.json
--- the human picks the yes option: accepted true
    000001-effort.opened.json
    000002-gate.answered.json
    {"by":"record-gate-answer.sh","body":{"record":"spec-approval","subject":"9f2c","question":"Approve this spec?","accept":"Approve the spec (Recommended)","answer":"Approve the spec (Recommended)","accepted":true}}
           0
--- the human types their own answer: accepted false
    {"answer":"Approve, but fix section 2 first","accepted":false}
--- an ordinary gate (no --record): no event
    events before        3, after        3
--- a subagent's answer: no event
    [no output]
--- only the hook may write gate.answered
    event-write.sh: gate.answered refused: gate.answered is written only by record-gate-answer.sh
    event-write.sh: gate.answered refused: accepted must say whether the answer is the accept option
--- junk input: exit 0
    [exit 0]
--- the shared reader: the newest answer counts
  spec-approval on 9f2c: the newest is the typed answer (no)
    gate-answer.sh: the newest answer (event 3) did not accept: Approve, but fix section 2 first
    [exit 1]
  then a yes: accepted
    ACCEPTED: 4
    [exit 0]
  then a no: the earlier yes no longer counts
    gate-answer.sh: the newest answer (event 5) did not accept: Change it
    [exit 1]
  another subject, and no answer at all
    gate-answer.sh: no answer for spec-approval on other
    [exit 1]
    gate-answer.sh: no answer for effort-start on 9f2c
    [exit 1]
